clang: the EmiBSD target, its predefined macros and C types

Why a patch: clang must know the target's C ABI to compile for it. EmiBSDTargetInfo
defines __EmiBSD__ (and nothing of any other system), `unix`, _REENTRANT with
-pthread, __STDC_NO_THREADS__ (the libc has no <threads.h>), __FLOAT128__ on
x86-64; the libc's types: wchar_t and wint_t int, int64_t and intmax_t long long
(also on AArch64, where the generic target would say long), the profiling entry
__mcount; malloc's 16-byte alignment. Registered for aarch64 and x86_64.
Written by EmiBSD (ISC); carried by DevTools over the pinned tag. Author: Emilio
Navarrete Lineros, 2026-10-31.

